---
import LegalLayout from '../components/layout/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site, emails } from '../data/site';

const toc = [
  { href: '#responsible', label: 'Who is responsible' },
  { href: '#summary', label: 'The short version' },
  { href: '#email', label: 'Information you send by email' },
  { href: '#purposes', label: 'How it is used' },
  { href: '#providers', label: 'Email providers' },
  { href: '#hosting', label: 'Hosting and technical data' },
  { href: '#cookies', label: 'Cookies and analytics' },
  { href: '#retention', label: 'How long it is kept' },
  { href: '#sharing', label: 'Sharing' },
  { href: '#requests', label: 'Your requests' },
  { href: '#links', label: 'Links to other sites' },
  { href: '#changes', label: 'Changes to this notice' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Obsidixz"
  description="How the Obsidixz parent website handles personal information: email correspondence, hosting logs, cookies and your requests."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  lede="This notice covers the Obsidixz parent website and the email route it provides. It describes what actually happens — including what this website does not do."
  updated={site.lastUpdated}
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="responsible">Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    Obsidixz is a parent brand described on this website. It is currently an unregistered business
    brand operated by <strong>{site.operator}</strong>, based in {site.locality}. That individual is
    responsible for the information described in this notice.
  </p>
  <p>
    For any question about this notice, or about information you have sent, write to
    <a href={`mailto:${emails.general}`}>{emails.general}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="summary">The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>This website has no enquiry form. Nothing is submitted through the site.</li>
    <li>There are no analytics, advertising or tracking scripts, and no embedded third-party media.</li>
    <li>When you email an Obsidixz address, your message is processed by your email provider and by
      Microsoft Outlook, which stores it.</li>
    <li>The site is served by GitHub Pages, which may record standard technical request information.</li>
    <li>A fixed retention period for the parent inbox has not yet been set. You can ask for your
      correspondence to be deleted.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="email">Information you send by email</h2>
  <p>
    The website itself does not collect personal information. Its contact actions open your own
    email application with an Obsidixz address filled in; the message is then sent by you, through
    your own provider.
  </p>
  <p>What arrives depends entirely on what you choose to include. Typically this is:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name and email address, and an organisation or role if you give one;</li>
    <li>the content of your message and any contact details you add to it;</li>
    <li>any attachment you decide to send;</li>
    <li>standard email metadata such as the time the message was sent.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Please do not send banking credentials, identity documents, passwords or other sensitive
    information in an initial enquiry.
  </p>

  <h2 id="purposes">How it is used</h2>
  <p>Information you send by email is used to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>read and answer your enquiry;</li>
    <li>keep a record of the correspondence so a conversation can be picked up later;</li>
    <li>pass the enquiry to the relevant Obsidixz business where that is clearly what you are asking
      for;</li>
    <li>comply with an obligation that applies to us, where one does.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Your information is not used for advertising, profiling or automated decision-making, and it is
    not added to a marketing list because you emailed.
  </p>

  <h2 id="providers">Email providers</h2>
  <p>
    Obsidixz addresses are Microsoft Outlook mailboxes. Microsoft processes, delivers and stores
    messages sent to them, including backups and technical logs, under its own terms and privacy
    statement. Your own email provider also processes the message before it reaches an Obsidixz
    inbox, and may do so in a different country.
  </p>
  <p>
    Those providers operate infrastructure this website cannot inspect or control. In particular, a
    copy of an email may remain in a provider's backups after a message has been deleted from a
    mailbox.
  </p>

  <h2 id="hosting">Hosting and technical data</h2>
  <p>
    This website is a static site served by GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc. (part of
    Microsoft). When a page is requested, GitHub's infrastructure processes the request and may
    record technical information such as the IP address, the browser or device type, the page
    requested and the time of the request, for delivery, security and abuse prevention. GitHub also
    provides repository owners with aggregated traffic information.
  </p>
  <p>
    This website installs no analytics service of its own and is not configured to collect or
    profile individual visitors. GitHub's handling of data is described in its own privacy
    statement: <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cookies">Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>
    This website sets no cookies of its own and loads no third-party fonts, scripts, pixels or
    embedded media. If infrastructure used to deliver the site sets a cookie, it is not controlled
    by this website.
  </p>
  <p>
    If analytics, cookies or embedded services are introduced later, this notice will be updated to
    describe what they are and what they collect. No such measurement is in place today.
  </p>

  <h2 id="retention">How long it is kept</h2>
  <p>
    Correspondence is kept for as long as it is useful to answer your enquiry and to keep a record
    of the conversation. A single fixed retention period for the parent inbox has not yet been
    adopted; when one is, it will be recorded on this page.
  </p>
  <p>
    You may ask for your correspondence to be deleted at any time. It will be deleted unless a
    specific legal or operational reason requires it to be kept — for example, an active matter or
    a record needed to answer a dispute. Copies held in a provider's backups may persist for a
    period outside the website's control.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sharing">Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    Information is not sold, rented or traded. It may be shared with the specific Obsidixz business
    your enquiry concerns, and with the providers described above that process email and hosting.
    It may be disclosed where the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="requests">Your requests</h2>
  <p>
    Write to <a href={`mailto:${emails.general}`}>{emails.general}</a> to ask what information is
    held about you, to have it corrected, or to ask for it to be deleted. Include enough detail to
    identify the correspondence. Requests are answered by hand; this website does not charge a fee
    for making one.
  </p>

  <h2 id="links">Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    This site links to the Obsidixz business websites and to email applications. Those destinations
    have their own privacy practices, and this notice applies only to the parent website at
    obsidixz.pp.ua.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes to this notice</h2>
  <p>
    This notice may be updated as the organisation develops or its tools change. The date at the top
    of this page shows the current version.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
